<title>CANADA: Canada to hold 5 bond auctions in Q2 1997.</title>
<headline>Canada to hold 5 bond auctions in Q2 1997.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada said on Thursday it will hold five bond auctions, including one real return issue, in the second quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>The first auction, of 30-year bonds, will be on April 23, with details to be released on April 17.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry said earlier today it would stop auctioning three-year government bonds.</p>
<p>Details follow.  </p>
<p> Term    Auction date  Details  Dated    Amt Maturing</p>
<p> 30-yr    Apr 23	 Apr 17   May 1	---------</p>
<p> 10-yr    May 7	  May 1    May 15     C$876 million</p>
<p> 5-yr     May 28	 May 22   June 2     ---------</p>
<p> RRB	June 4	 May 29   June 9     ---------</p>
<p> 2-yr     June 11	June 5   June 16    ---------</p>
<p>The real return bond is auctioned on a single-price format.</p>
<p>((-- Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
</text>
